        "original_id": "27d39423-173d-5b17-a5cd-4ab75cee5134",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Modern Music, Modern Records\n- People: Bihari brothers, Little Richard, Etta James, Joe Houston, Ike Turner, Tina Turner, John Lee Hooker, Richard Wayne Penniman\n- Places: Los Angeles\n- Topics: R&B, American record labels\n\nFacts:\n- Modern Music was an American record company and label formed in 1945 in Los Angeles by the Bihari brothers.\n- In the 1950s and 1960s, Modern Records was one of the major R&B labels.\n- In the 1950s and 1960s, Modern Records had artists including Etta James, Joe Houston, Little Richard, Ike and Tina Turner, and John Lee Hooker.\n- Richard Wayne Penniman was born on December 5, 1932.\n- Richard Wayne Penniman was known as Little Richard.\n- Little Richard was an American musician, singer, actor, comedian, and songwriter.",
